#                        3 fixtures agree on COUNT; on path+host; NOT on the timestamp; and
#                        a row with no member field reads None, not 0
#     2  member-source  a 200 row supplies the count; a lone 502 supplies None, not 0
#     5  refuses        5 synthetic rows the reader must raise Unreadable on
#     3  exhaustiveness empty population derives {} not a verdict; an all-controls crawl
#                        yields no verdict; row arithmetic is an int comparison
#     2  integration    unreadable row in a real 40-row ledger: refuses to emit, and
#                        --allow-unreadable records it rather than dropping it
#     8  population R1  the rule that produced this pass's most consequential finding
